// @name: MIDI channel override
// @tagline: address in the language, per-note override
// @description: Two MIDI actors declare their channel in BPScript (transport.midi(ch:N)); one note carries an inline (ch:5) override. The output address travels in the scene, not via any host routing map (KAI-9 test scene).
// @language: bpscript
// @outputs: midi
// @level: advanced
// @tags: orchestration, multi-actor, midi, routing
//
// KAN KAI-9 — test scene: address-in-the-language + inline channel override.
//
// Both actors declare their OUTPUT ADDRESS in BPScript (transport.midi(ch:N)) — the
// host invents no routing. `lead` plays on MIDI channel 1, `bass` on channel 2.
// The note `lead.E4(ch:5)` carries an INLINE CHANNEL OVERRIDE: that single note jumps
// to channel 5, the rest of `lead` stays on its declared channel 1.
//
// The note is PREFIXED (`lead.E4`), NOT nude (`E4`) — required, not stylistic (décision
// Romain 2026-07-03, hub/decisions/2026-07-03-note-nue-ch-implique-sortie-midi.md). With
// TWO western actors the actor of a nude note is AMBIGUOUS, so its output layer isn't
// graven and the note is dropped from MIDI; the prefix names the actor, and Kairos then
// graves channel 5 end-to-end. (An earlier comment here wrongly called the nude form
// "canon" — it is not.)
//
// FLAT sequence (`S -> Lead Low`), NOT braces `{ }`: the inline `(ch:N)` override is
// rejected inside `{ }` by the current parser (bug, routed to bpscript — architecte
// msg [297]). The simultaneous `{ Lead, Low }` form (without override) is the separate
// 2-actor→2-output routing case.
//
// Purpose: exercise the KAI-9 big-bang — once Kairos materializes the output layer
// from the tree (and the host drops pickTransport / the actor→transport map), this
// scene proves the per-actor address AND the per-note override travel in the tree,
// not via any host-side routing map.

@core
@tempo:120

@actor lead  @alphabet.western  transport.midi(ch:1)
@actor bass  @alphabet.western  transport.midi(ch:2)

S -> Lead Low

Lead -> lead.C4 lead.E4(ch:5) lead.G4 lead.C4
Low  -> bass.C2 bass.G2 bass.C2 bass.E2
